WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:29.860
Google's first orbital ai satellite will test whether chips can shed heat in vacuum aboard a SpaceX launch next week. This is Spacex Daily, episode 111. Spacex completed propellant loading and launch day procedures on September 24 for Starship Flight 14 without igniting engines. The target profile calls for orbital insertion, six earth orbits, and deployment of 26 next generation starlink satellites. The super heavy booster is

00:00:29.860 --> 00:00:35.040
planned to splash down in the Gulf of Mexico while the ship upper-stage re-enters in the Pacific

00:00:35.040 --> 00:00:42.180
west of Chile. The launch window opened September 28th at 5.45 pm Indian Standard Time from

00:00:42.180 --> 00:00:49.060
Starbase, Texas. NASA awarded SpaceX nearly $1 billion for three additional crew rotation flights

00:00:49.060 --> 00:00:54.900
to the International Space Station. The contract extends SpaceX support for the station through at

00:00:54.900 --> 00:01:01.400
2030. A refurbished dragon capsule reached pad 40 at Cape Canaveral and will mate with

00:01:01.400 --> 00:01:07.040
a third flight Falcon 9 booster. Commander Jessica Watkins will lead pilot Luke Delaney

00:01:07.040 --> 00:01:13.420
plus mission specialists Joshua Kutrick and Sergei Teteriatnikov. Dawking is targeted

00:01:13.420 --> 00:01:20.080
for 8 p.m. Eastern daylight time on the October 1 launch day. NASA selected Kayla Berkin as

00:01:20.080 --> 00:01:25.940
spacecraft commander for the Crew-14 mission, with Chris Birch as pilot, Jaxa Astronaut

00:01:25.940 --> 00:01:30.480
Makoto Sua, and Ross Cosmos Cosmonaut Arutuyun Kivirian.

00:01:31.320 --> 00:01:36.840
Baron previously flew on Crew-3 in 2021, and will return for a second mission while the

00:01:36.840 --> 00:01:38.980
other three will make their first space flights.

00:01:39.620 --> 00:01:45.820
The crew will join Expedition-75-76 and conduct science experiments during a long duration

00:01:45.820 --> 00:01:46.280
stay.

00:01:46.280 --> 00:01:52.200
Google's project Suncatcher prototype will fly on the transporter 18 ride share next week.

00:01:52.680 --> 00:01:57.640
The satellite will test Trillium TPUs in orbit, collecting data on launch vibration,

00:01:58.020 --> 00:01:59.920
radiation, and thermal performance.

00:02:00.540 --> 00:02:05.640
It will run Gemini models in 15-minute bursts followed by radiator cool-down periods,

00:02:06.080 --> 00:02:11.540
with a 2027 follow-on mission planned to test laser links between two satellites.

00:02:11.540 --> 00:02:14.360
Starlink Mobile has launched in Uganda.

00:02:15.000 --> 00:02:17.420
The rollout occurred through an air-tub partnership.

00:02:17.980 --> 00:02:21.700
The service provides direct-to-cell connectivity to users in Uganda.

00:02:22.240 --> 00:02:25.440
This rollout expands Starlink's carrier partner model.

00:02:25.820 --> 00:02:28.860
The model focuses on mobile coverage in additional markets.

00:02:29.580 --> 00:02:32.300
Reports on the launch come from bassnor.com.

00:02:32.780 --> 00:02:35.560
The partnership enables connectivity for local users.

00:02:36.300 --> 00:02:39.920
SpaceX has secured a classified orbital tracking contract.

00:02:39.920 --> 00:02:43.560
The award supports national security tracking capabilities.

00:02:44.140 --> 00:02:47.440
This development arrives as Starship Flight 14 approaches.

00:02:48.140 --> 00:02:50.060
Details on the contract remain limited.

00:02:50.580 --> 00:02:53.500
The limitation stems from the classified nature of the work.

00:02:54.080 --> 00:02:58.220
Information on the award appears in adhoc-news.de.

00:02:58.900 --> 00:03:02.020
The contract bolsters orbital tracking for security needs.

00:03:02.640 --> 00:03:06.440
Reddit users are discussing a mid-October drive from Denver to Starbase.

00:03:06.440 --> 00:03:10.000
The discussion centers on whether the trip remains worthwhile.

00:03:10.560 --> 00:03:14.120
The concern arises if most hardware has already rolled to the pad.

00:03:14.820 --> 00:03:18.060
Another thread highlights the October 1st Florida double header.

00:03:18.660 --> 00:03:22.440
Crew 13 is listed at 11.10 a.m. Eastern Daylight Time.

00:03:23.020 --> 00:03:29.100
An N-R-O-L 97 Falcon Heavy follows at 11.53 p.m. Eastern Daylight Time.

00:03:29.800 --> 00:03:33.380
Observers note the potential for three booster landings in 12 hours.

00:03:33.380 --> 00:03:36.280
Both threads draw from reddit.com.

00:03:36.520 --> 00:03:41.420
One thing worth watching is the pace of Starship Flight 14 regulatory approvals.

00:03:41.960 --> 00:03:47.480
The FAA license remains pending even after the wet dress rehearsal, and any extension

00:03:47.480 --> 00:03:51.640
would push the first orbital attempt beyond the current September 28 window.

00:03:52.280 --> 00:03:57.580
On the AI front, the live threads to watch are Starlink Direct to Cell expansion and Orbital

00:03:57.580 --> 00:03:58.720
Compute Demonstrations.

00:03:58.720 --> 00:03:58.900
engines.

00:03:59.400 --> 00:04:04.240
From an engineering standpoint, removing air as a heat transfer medium forces a complete

00:04:04.240 --> 00:04:06.900
redesign of how processors reject waste heat.

00:04:07.520 --> 00:04:12.460
On the ground, forced air cooling moves heat at rates set by fan speed and surface area.

00:04:12.920 --> 00:04:17.940
But in orbit, the only path left is radiation through pipes and deployable panels whose

00:04:17.940 --> 00:04:20.740
effectiveness scales with the fourth power of temperature.

00:04:21.360 --> 00:04:27.620
The sun-catcher prototype therefore cycles its TPUs on for 15 minutes and then idols while

00:04:27.620 --> 00:04:33.380
radiators shed stored energy. A duty cycle chosen because continuous operation would exceed

00:04:33.380 --> 00:04:38.680
the thermal mass available before the next eclipse. Early chamber tests already showed

00:04:38.680 --> 00:04:44.660
the pipes can move the expected kilowatt load, yet orbital data will reveal how microvibrations

00:04:44.660 --> 00:04:50.780
and proton damage alter emissivity over weeks. If the radiators maintain margin, the same

00:04:50.780 --> 00:04:55.860
architecture could support larger clusters whose power budget comes from near continuous sunlight,

00:04:55.860 --> 00:04:59.500
rather than ground-based solar farms limited to daylight hours.

00:05:00.020 --> 00:05:06.320
The next milestone, laser-linked pairs in 2027 will test whether data movement

00:05:06.320 --> 00:05:11.420
between nodes adds its own heat load that the same radiator set must also reject.

00:05:12.100 --> 00:05:15.480
A quick look at the tape shows the stock closing modestly higher.

00:05:15.980 --> 00:05:20.180
Before we go, the transporter 18 ride share next week will carry the first

00:05:20.180 --> 00:05:23.960
project Suncatcher prototype among its small satellite manifest.

00:05:24.560 --> 00:05:26.680
That's your SpaceX news for today.

